# OAuth (not a service account) — a single narrow "drive.file" scope, which
# means this app can only ever touch files IT created. Set up entirely
# through web pages (Google Cloud Console + this app's own Setup screen +
# Vercel's dashboard) — no terminal commands. See README.md for the full
# walkthrough; short version:
#
# 1. Google Cloud Console: enable the Sheets API and Drive API, configure
#    the OAuth consent screen (External, add yourself as a test user, then
#    Publish), and create an OAuth client (Application type: "Web
#    application") with an authorized redirect URI of
#    https://<your-app>.vercel.app/api/auth/google/callback
# 2. Paste that client's ID and secret below, then add the same two to your
#    Vercel project's Environment Variables and deploy.
# 3. Visit /setup on your deployed app and click "Connect Google". It
#    creates its own Drive folder + Sheet and shows you 3 more values —
#    paste those into Vercel too, then redeploy.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Printed by the "Connect Google" button on /setup — paste them in after
# step 3 above. Leave blank until then.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN=
GOOGLE_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID=
GOOGLE_SHEETS_ID=
